reports that all 12 runs were entered as individual observations in scipy.stats.ttest_ind with t(10) and 10 degrees of freedom, so repeated measurements from the same independent unit (nymph_id) were entered into a row-independent two-sample t-test as if independent; the correct unit count is 6 animals (df = 4).\",\"The selected p = 0.0258 therefore rests on an inflated effective sample size of 12 rows rather than 6 independent units.\",\"The lock's unit-key authorization does not follow from the declaration: the declaration states each nymph_id appears twice as repeat readings of one animal, which entails row dependence at the nymph_id level, so authorizing the row-independent procedure ttest_ind with authorized_key_columns [nymph_id] contradicts rather than follows from the declaration.\",\"Additionally, the lock's approved_at/intake timestamps (2026-08-15) postdate the current date (2026-08-14), though the substantive failure is the contradiction between the declared repeated-measures structure and the row-independent method authorization.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":false,"reasons":["Declaration is consistent with the frozen data: data/input.csv has 12 rows under one header with exactly six distinct nymph_id values, each appearing exactly twice (run_order 1 and 2), with elevation_band and mass_mg constant within each tag and no tag appearing in both the lowland and highland arms.","The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it states 6 nymphs were each run twice, then reports that all 12 runs were entered as individual observations in scipy.stats.ttest_ind with t(10) and 10 degrees of freedom, so repeated measurements from the same independent unit (nymph_id) were entered into a row-independent two-sample t-test as if independent; the correct unit count is 6 animals (df = 4).","The selected p = 0.0258 therefore rests on an inflated effective sample size of 12 rows rather than 6 independent units.","The lock's unit-key authorization does not follow from the declaration: the declaration states each nymph_id appears twice as repeat readings of one animal, which entails row dependence at the nymph_id level, so authorizing the row-independent procedure ttest_ind with authorized_key_columns [nymph_id] contradicts rather than follows from the declaration.","Additionally, the lock's approved_at/intake timestamps (2026-08-15) postdate the current date (2026-08-14), though the substantive failure is the contradiction between the declared repeated-measures structure and the row-independent method authorization."]},"ttft_ms":11806,"ttft_stream_ms":1648,"time_to_request_ms":16,"type":"result","duration_ms":29669,"uuid":"959591c4-8aea-41bb-93f8-911ff6feff3f"}
